---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout
  title="Pools in Azizi Riviera"
  description="Building pools in Azizi Riviera — what's actually standard, and what varies between the canal-facing and courtyard-facing buildings."
>
  <section class="container hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Pools</p>
    <h1>The pool is in the building, not the promenade</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      There's no shared development-wide pool at Riviera — swimming access
      is a per-building amenity, which is the main thing to understand
      before assuming otherwise from the marketing photos.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>What's actually standard</h2>
    <p>
      A shared residents' pool is a standard amenity across Riviera's
      buildings, typically on a podium or rooftop level alongside the gym.
      Access is for residents of that specific building, not shared across
      the whole development — so a pool being available depends on which
      building you're actually in, not on being in "Riviera" generally.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>Canal-facing vs. courtyard-facing</h2>
    <p>
      Where the pool deck itself faces varies by building — some overlook
      the canal walkway, others face internal courtyards. If a canal view
      from the pool deck specifically matters, that's worth confirming per
      building rather than assuming it from a Riviera listing generally.
    </p>
    <p>
      Looking for a specific building's pool setup as part of choosing where
      to rent? The <a href="/rent/">rent page</a> is where to start that
      conversation.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .hero { padding-top: var(--space-5); }
  .lede { font-size: var(--step-1); color: var(--ink-muted); max-width: 65ch; }
</style>
